## Service Registration

- Register singletons for shared instances
- Register factories for per-request instances
- Use generic types for type safety
- Log service registration events
- Check registration before usage

```dart
// Register singleton service
ServiceLocator.instance.registerSingleton<ApiService>(
  ApiServiceImpl(),
);

// Register factory for new instances
ServiceLocator.instance.registerFactory<UserRepository>(
  () => UserRepositoryImpl(),
);
```

## Service Retrieval

- Use generic get method
- Handle unregistered service exceptions
- Check registration with isRegistered
- Avoid direct constructor dependencies
- Retrieve services at usage point

```dart
// Get service instance
final ApiService apiService = ServiceLocator.instance.get<ApiService>();

// Check if registered
if (ServiceLocator.instance.isRegistered<DatabaseService>()) {
  // Use service
}
```

## Service Locator Implementation

- Singleton pattern for locator instance
- Type-safe service storage maps
- Separate singleton and factory storage
- Clear debugging with Logger
- Exception for unregistered services

```dart
// @lib/services/service_locator.dart
class ServiceLocator {
  static final ServiceLocator _instance = ServiceLocator._();
  static ServiceLocator get instance => _instance;

  final Map<Type, dynamic> _services = {};
  final Map<Type, dynamic Function()> _factories = {};
}
```

## Lifecycle Management

- Initialize services in main function
- Register core services first
- Register feature services after
- Clear services for testing
- Unregister when not needed

```dart
// Initialize in main.dart
Future<void> setupServices() async {
  ServiceLocator.instance
    ..registerSingleton<Logger>(LoggerImpl())
    ..registerSingleton<DatabaseService>(DatabaseServiceImpl())
    ..registerFactory<ApiService>(() => ApiServiceImpl());
}
```

## Interface Registration

- Register interfaces not implementations
- Use abstract base classes
- Enable dependency inversion principle
- Support multiple implementations
- Facilitate testing with mocks

```dart
// Register interface
ServiceLocator.instance.registerSingleton<BaseService>(
  ConcreteServiceImpl(),
);

// Get through interface
final BaseService service = ServiceLocator.instance.get<BaseService>();
```

## Testing Support

- Clear all services before tests
- Register mock services for testing
- Use factories for test doubles
- Isolate service dependencies
- Reset state between tests

```dart
// In test setup
setUp(() {
  ServiceLocator.instance.clear();
  ServiceLocator.instance.registerSingleton<ApiService>(
    MockApiService(),
  );
});
```

## Service Organization

- Core services in @lib/services/implementations
- Service interfaces in @lib/services/interfaces
- Feature services within feature modules
- Base service interface for lifecycle
- Consistent naming conventions

## Error Handling

- Throw exceptions for unregistered services
- Log registration and retrieval events
- Validate service types at registration
- Handle circular dependencies gracefully
- Provide clear error messages

```dart
// Service not found exception
throw Exception('Service of type ${T.toString()} is not registered');
```

## Best Practices

- Keep service locator lightweight
- Avoid service locator in domain layer
- Use dependency injection over service locator
- Register services at application startup
- Document service dependencies clearly